# App acceptance criteria

- Follow APP-STANDARDS.md and standards/requirements.json on every update.
- Maintain evidence and unchecked gaps in APP-COMPLIANCE.md; instructions alone
  never establish implemented features, native support or a verified release.
- Use TMA-Finance Settings layout for every app and theme. Keep feature, bug,
  issue and Help actions on main Settings, with settings/optional KB search.
- Default to Original Bubble Look. Implement/verify/push one theme per app update
  before the next: Bubble, Finance, ArtCraft-inspired, then Blocky Basic.
- Preserve approved identities; Agent Office is grey with a white robot.
- Offer first-setup tours/replay with visible unblurred targets and adjacent dialogs.
- Follow the profile, sounds, appearance, accessibility, connectivity, crash-report,
  notifications, tray, New Features and zero-cost requirements in the standards.
- Record actual OS versions/architectures and packaged test evidence. Distinguish
  unsupported OS, known unsupported version and not-yet-verified versions.
- Review README.md and SECURITY.md after every branch update. Record assessment;
  preserve accurate app-specific security models and release approval rules.
- Update affected KB/tours/release notes; follow kb-maintenance.mdc and review all
  outgoing artifacts under security-data.mdc before publication.
- Run meaningful functional/performance checks for every code update. Record a
  no-runtime-impact assessment for policy-only changes; do not invent test results.
- Copy standards, evidence checklist, AGENTS and security/KB rules to future apps.
- Defer licensing, usage-rights/legality and legal-policy work per owner direction.
- Prepare startup-animation proposals for owner approval before implementing them.
